All three subfactions are written. Here's a summary of what was added to `Subfactions.md`:

**Voidfarers** — The explorers and wanderers. Built the waymarkers, scattered the seeds, crewed the research vessels. Their augmentations are tuned for deep space. In the End of All Things, they're scattered across the galaxy running dark — the eyes and ears of a species in hiding, carrying messages between the fragments of a dying civilization.

**Cradle** — The keepers of community and home. After the Folly unmade the original cradle worlds, they became stewards of grief — remembering what was loved without reaching for what was gone. They organized the seclusion in the void and maintain the identity of the species across geological time. Most deeply intertwined with the Law's spell beyond spells, making their enclaves disproportionately dangerous.

**The Lost and the Damned** — The Gardeners who stayed behind when the rest retreated. Scattered in ones and twos across the galaxy, hidden among Stewards and Torn, their identities concealed. Every one of them is a walking weapon — the dying Law channels the energy of harnessed stars through any threatened Gardener. They fight with precision and restraint because escalation means catastrophic detonation. The Torn Uprising caught many of them between sides.

All changes are uncommitted for your review. One note: the existing Lawmakers entry has an incomplete sentence ("lost touch with .") — pre-existing, not introduced here.

